{
  "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
  "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Ms. Campbell)",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When an officer makes a traffic stop, activates his flashing lights, he seizes not only the driver of the car but also the car and every person and everything in that car."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And would that apply if a bus was pulled over?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, are you saying then that in a case in which the bus is stopped, the car is stopped and so on, the role for the test about whether a reasonable person would regard himself as free to leave is a test to determine when the, when the seizure ends, as distinct from when the seizure begins?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Campbell",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the passenger is certainly stopped when the car comes to a halt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would still say that the passenger is seized when the car comes to a stop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What about a shutdown of an airport?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF CLIFFORD E. ZALL\nON BEHALF OF RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Clifford E. Zall",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view that does not result in a seizure of a passenger."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Have you ever been stopped?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It may be that you can walk away, you're not in an enclosed space. Suppose the passenger knows when the police approaches: Oh my goodness, I didn't buckle up. Would that passenger be the object of the police authority from the start?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Going back to Justice Stevens' question, the passenger knows the minute the red light goes on that the police can either tell them to get out or tell him to stay in. He knows at that very moment. That seems to me to substantially limit his freedom of action and indicates that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're saying he doesn't have actual authority. If I understand you, you're saying he has no authority to stop an innocent passenger from walking away. Aren't you saying that? Unless there's some reason to hold a person in the car, he has no authority to stop him from walking away."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ZALL",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think that even were this Court to rule that the passenger were subject to a seizure, that the presence of the arrest warrant attenuates any taint and therefore the evidence was -- was not suppressible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. CAMPBELL",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because Your Honor, this Court has -- this Court held in Delaware versus Prouse, the Court recognized the passengers as well as drivers have a liberty interest in free travel on the highways, and because if we look at every case this Court has decided in the last 20 or 30 years regarding when a seizure occurs, the case of a passenger in an auto test -- in an auto stop meets the test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1a81ac5b64a019dd75a5f3c849fb110f428b8e260b5a487e2add7b75973d29a9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1a81ac5b64a0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just to address for a moment whether or not remand is appropriate in this case, just to clarify the procedural posture."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-06-8120",
      "confidence": 0.0,
